claim.claim-text:
a cam body having an axis of rotation;
a plurality of cam surfaces extending around said cam body, each said cam surface comprising a respective region of increasing radius, said radii being measured from and about said axis of rotation, all of said cam surfaces being circumferentially aligned with one another;
a respective discontinuity of said cam surfaces being positioned between each of said cam surfaces;
at least one stop surface projecting from said cam body transversely to said axis of rotation, said stop surface being positioned adjacent to one of said respective discontinuities of said cam surfaces.

a plurality of traction surfaces extending around said cam body, each said traction surface comprising a plurality of projections extending transversely to said axis of rotation; and
a respective gap in said traction surfaces being positioned between each of said traction surfaces, each said gap being aligned axially with a respective discontinuity of said cam surface;
more preferably

wherein the cam further comprises
a plurality of traction surfaces extending around said cam body, each said traction surface comprising a plurality of projections extending transversely to said axis of rotation; and
a respective gap in said traction surfaces being positioned between each of said traction surfaces, each said gap being aligned axially with a respective discontinuity of said cam surface;
a gear mounted on said cam body coaxially with said axis of rotation;
wherein said cam surfaces are positioned between said gear and said traction surfaces;
preferably wherein said cam surfaces are positioned proximate to said traction surfaces, or wherein said at least one stop surface is positioned between said gear and said cam surfaces.
